# TuningFork, the Strudel way

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:tuning_fork, "~> 0.1.4"},
  {:tuning_fork_samples, "~> 0.1.4"},
  {:tuning_fork_kino, "~> 0.1.4"}
])
```

## Paste and play

A **TF Patterns** cell takes a piece from strudel.cc as it is written: `$:` rows, method
chains, `let` variables, `setcps`, `samples('github:…')`. Press **Evaluate** (or ctrl+enter)
and it plays; the cps field takes the tempo the piece sets. A word it cannot read is
reported under its line.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoTuningFork.LivePatternsCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
unless Process.whereis(TuningFork.Stage), do: Kino.render(KinoTuningFork.stage())

rows = [
  %{source: "// \"coastline\" @by eddyflux"},
  %{source: "// @version 1.0"},
  %{source: "samples('github:eddyflux/crate')"},
  %{source: "setcps(.75)"},
  %{source: "let chords = chord(\"<Bbm9 Fm9>/4\").dict('ireal')"},
  %{source: "stack("},
  %{source: "  stack( // DRUMS"},
  %{source: "    s(\"bd\").struct(\"<[x*<1 2> [~@3 x]] x>\"),"},
  %{source: "    s(\"~ [rim, sd:<2 3>]\").room(\"<0 .2>\"),"},
  %{source: "    n(\"[0 <1 3>]*<2!3 4>\").s(\"hh\"),"},
  %{source: "    s(\"rd:<1!3 2>*2\").mask(\"<0 0 1 1>/16\").gain(.5)"},
  %{source: "  ).bank('crate')"},
  %{source: "  .mask(\"<[0 1] 1 1 1>/16\".early(.5))"},
  %{source: "  , // CHORDS"},
  %{source: "  chords.offset(-1).voicing().s(\"gm_epiano1:1\")"},
  %{source: "  .phaser(4).room(.5)"},
  %{source: "  , // MELODY"},
  %{source: "  n(\"<0!3 1*2>\").set(chords).mode(\"root:g2\")"},
  %{source: "  .voicing().s(\"gm_acoustic_bass\"),"},
  %{source: "  chords.n(\"[0 <4 3 <2 5>>*2](<3 5>,8)\")"},
  %{source: "  .anchor(\"D5\").voicing()"},
  %{source: "  .segment(4).clip(rand.range(.4,.8))"},
  %{source: "  .room(.75).shape(.3).delay(.25)"},
  %{source: "  .fm(sine.range(3,8).slow(8))"},
  %{source: "  .lpf(sine.range(500,1000).slow(8)).lpq(5)"},
  %{source: "  .rarely(ply(\"2\")).chunk(4, fast(2))"},
  %{source: "  .gain(perlin.range(.6, .9))"},
  %{source: "  .mask(\"<0 1 1 0>/16\")"},
  %{source: ")"},
  %{source: ".late(\"[0 .01]*4\").late(\"[0 .01]*2\").size(4)"}
]

pattern = TuningFork.Session.combined(rows)

if TuningFork.Stage.cycle() do
  TuningFork.Stage.update_pattern(pattern, at: :cycle)
else
  TuningFork.Stage.start_pattern(pattern, cps: 0.75)
end
```

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoTuningFork.LivePatternsCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
unless Process.whereis(TuningFork.Stage), do: Kino.render(KinoTuningFork.stage())

rows = [
  %{source: "setcps(.5)"},
  %{source: "$: s(\"bd*2, hh*4, ~ sd\").gain(.8)"},
  %{source: "$: note(\"<c2 eb2 g2 bb2>*2\").s(\"gm_acoustic_bass\").clip(.8)"},
  %{
    source:
      "$: n(\"<0 2 4 7>*4\").scale(\"c:minor\").s(\"gm_epiano1\").room(.3).gain(perlin.range(.5,.8))"
  }
]

pattern = TuningFork.Session.combined(rows)

if TuningFork.Stage.cycle() do
  TuningFork.Stage.update_pattern(pattern, at: :cycle)
else
  TuningFork.Stage.start_pattern(pattern, cps: 0.5)
end
```

## Coastline, by eddyflux

The piece as published, with its sample pack. `samples('github:eddyflux/crate')` fetches
`strudel.json` from the repo and each recording the first time it is played, so the first
evaluate needs the network and takes a moment. The drums are masked until cycle 8 and the
melody until cycle 16 — at 0.75 cps that is ten and twenty seconds of chords first, as on
strudel.cc.

## The same from code

`TuningFork.Strudel` is what the cell uses. `to_rows/1` shows the translation, and
`pattern/1` gives a pattern to start on a stage.

```elixir
KinoTuningFork.stage()
```

```elixir
js = """
setcps(.5)
$: s("bd*2, hh*4, ~ sd").gain(.8)
$: note("<c2 eb2 g2 bb2>*2").s("gm_acoustic_bass").clip(.8)
$: n("<0 2 4 7>*4").scale("c:minor").s("gm_epiano1").room(.3).gain(perlin.range(.5,.8))
"""

{:ok, rows} = TuningFork.Strudel.to_rows(js)
IO.puts(Enum.join(rows, "\n"))
```

```elixir
{:ok, pattern} = TuningFork.Strudel.pattern(js)
TuningFork.Stage.start_pattern(pattern, cps: 0.5)
```

```elixir
TuningFork.Stage.stop_pattern()
```
